  "output": {
    "answer": "The record doesn't say who plays the personas mechanically, but slide 16 calls the walk-through 'simulated, not human' — so the DONE/NOT calls came from an agent running the panel, not people. On rubber-stamping specifically: the verdict format forces every persona to name one concrete thing to cut, on a DONE verdict too, which is stated as the thing that keeps the panel from just rubber-stamping. Beyond that, and beyond how the panel's viewport or context was actually configured, that's not in the record — and the gate still missed a real-device failure the panel didn't catch, which is why the real device check stays a required last step.",
